    "title": "Three Men Charged with Attempted Murder in Shooting of Indiana Judge",
    "text": "• Three men were charged with attempted murder in connection with the shooting of Indiana Judge Steven Meyer and his wife.\n• The shooting occurred at their home in Lafayette on January 18.\n• Thomas Moss, one of the suspects, was scheduled to stand trial in Judge Meyer's court on unrelated violent felonies two days after the shooting.\n• Prosecutors allege Moss and the other two men conspired to target the judge.\n• Judge Meyer set Moss's bond at $3 million.\n• Raylen Ferguson's bond was set at a multi-million dollar amount, and he is alleged to have fired the shots.\n• Blake Smith's bond was set at a multi-million dollar amount, and he is accused of buying the gun.\n• Both Ferguson and Smith requested public defenders.\n• Amanda Milsap was arrested for allegedly trying to bribe a witness in Moss's case; her bond was set at $500,000.\n• Zenada Greer was arrested in Kentucky on obstruction and assisting a criminal charges and is awaiting extradition.\n• A Cass County judge was appointed by the Indiana Supreme Court to oversee the case.\n• A tentative trial date of May 6 has been set.",
    "summary": "Tippecanoe County Judge Steven Meyer and his wife, Kimberly, were wounded in a shooting at their home in Lafayette on Jan. 18. Prosecutors accused Moss and the two other men, with whom he allegedly shares gang ties, of conspiring to target the judge as part of a \"concerted effort to impede the proceedings.\" Multimillion-dollar bonds were also set for Raylen Ferguson, who is alleged to have fired the shots through Meyer's door, and Blake Smith, who is accused of buying the gun used in the shooting.",
